{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1382324-targeted-control-gravity","id":1382324,"title":"Targeted Control Gravity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-18T06:31:01-07:00","id":1382324,"title":"Targeted Control Gravity","content":"Is there a way to adjust the CG spell so that only the target is affected? When I first read the spell I imagined it worked like the gravitation \u201cLashings\u201d from the Stormlight Archives, allowing the caster to redirect how gravity affected themselves or something they touch. It essentially grants a form of flight whereby you Lash yourself in the direction you want to go and then fall that way. RAW CG affects an area, but through Reach or Improvised Casting would you allow this alteration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T09:29:15-07:00","id":1382339,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. Hmm, if I wanted to stick to just the original spell though, what I'd do is keep it an area of effect spell, but only make the area size 5 and centered on myself so it moves with me. Since that's viable, then just being able to cast it on yourself should also be viable I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T09:46:12-07:00","id":1382341,"title":"","content":"To take it a step further, could this become a touch attack spell? Grant the target a Withstand rating and if you pass it, they fall in whatever direction you choose. This becomes incredibly deadly, but then plenty of spells are deadly even at 2 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T10:14:45-07:00","id":1382343,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T10:47:10-07:00","id":1382348,"title":"","content":"I would have a targeted <i>Control Gravity</i> withstood by Stamina and, if there were handholds, give the victim a reflexive Dexterity or Wits + Athletics - Potency roll to grab on to something.<br /> <br /> Lashings, at least multiple lashings, would be more of a Forces 3 thing with <i>Gravitic Supremacy</i> or <i>Telekinesis</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:07:31-07:00","id":1383231,"title":"","content":"So apparently by RAW I can totally do this through Creative Thaumaturgy. I've been working through the book piecemeal and just now read that section. xD I'll bring this up to my ST next time we talk, but before I do I want to clarify if by RAW a custom spell that a Mage invents through CT can become a Praxis through repeated use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:42:20-07:00","id":1383236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1382324-targeted-control-gravity?p=1383231#post1383231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll bring this up to my ST next time we talk, but before I do I want to clarify if by RAW a custom spell that a Mage invents through CT can become a Praxis through repeated use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Everything that isn't a Rote or a Praxis is an improvised spell and Rotes and Praxes are mutually exclusive in application. Creative Thaumaturgy de facto makes improvised spells, and the other two types of spell are the result of repeated casting; nothing about the way the game works suggests there isn't a viable throughline from custom casting to codified mudra or signature spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T17:55:34-07:00","id":1383255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1382324-targeted-control-gravity?p=1383236#post1383236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Everything that isn't a Rote or a Praxis is an improvised spell and Rotes and Praxes are mutually exclusive in application. Creative Thaumaturgy de facto makes improvised spells, and the other two types of spell are the result of repeated casting; nothing about the way the game works suggests there isn't a viable throughline from custom casting to codified mudra or signature spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on that: <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> implies the exact opposite <i>vis a vis</i> praxes, with your first praxis after Awakening being an improvised spell that achieves three successes that the player spends a point of Willpower to turn into a praxis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}